So. Got an elven priest ascended: Father McGruder, kicking ass for the
lord :) Wishless, Genocideless, Elberethless too.

The last priest had crashed on the Quest and left no recovery stuff...
After that, Famine (of all enemies) got a Tourist on the way to the
right altar. Which kept me from playing a while.

Well, no matter, after a while I got bored, started a priest and it went 
rather well this time (took a week and a half of playing though).

Funny stuff included offering the Wizard of Yendor
to Susanowo (Samurai Pantheon) on the way back up.

Went from XL16 to XL17 from killing monsters alone.

Got my one and only BoH from a store in Orcus Town. Had used an
oilskin sack before.

First ascension using Stormbringer as a main weapon and not getting
killed by a priest or shopkeeper or something like that.
Got crowned around turn 39000 and received Stormbringer. Which, in
respect of serious damage, is somewhat lacking compared to, say,
#twoweaping Snickersnee and a Katana, let alone Grayswandir, but
the level-drain effect makes up for it when it matters (mainly
against priests and certain Wizard-types).

I'm still wondering what a good weapon for a priest would be, if
it isn't Stormbringer. Priest can only get to basic in Stormbringers
weapon class and Expert-mazing doesn't do nearly enough damage...

A scene upon arrival in the Wizards Tower involving around 10 or
  12 mariliths who summoned each other to the party (amongst other
  demons and monsters).

Vibrating square on Dlvl 51, So lowest Dlvl was 52.

Rodney fihgting the High Priest for the AoY.

Rodney double troubling and his clone masquerading as another monster, 
resulting in "Wait! That's the Wizard of Yendor!" messages. Most 
confusing that.

And having the AoY stolen on Water, where it got dropped beneath a
boulder. Took sometime to realize this, take of the RoLev, move the
boulder and go on.

No method of finding the portals on the Plains. Had one ?oGD in a
stash someplace and had polymorphed a crystal ball into a key or
something (hoping for a magic marker). I'd have thought either
magic mapping or confused detect treasure would do the trick, but
no luck... Which ment earth took a long time, fire was faster but
more, hmm, "exciting", what whith Archons summoning monsters, Rodney
double troubling... Luckily I could take refuge on the north border
of the Plane, between some lava and the edge, so the monsters only
came from two directions. WoTeleport, those are cool and were what
got me anywhere at all. Truly very cool, also nice on Astral.

Water took ages, had to do the AoY portal detection thingy. Air was
tough because of the elementals, but the portal was quickly found
once I got to the east side of the Plane. Nice vortices (and one
blessed diluted !oFH) got me through.


Used another !oFH on Astral. Left was Famine, got out 5 K-rations,
went there, altar of Amaterasu Omikami. Went back, middle altar,
Pestilence. Once I got in a hit or two, Pestilence was actually dead,
but I spend quite a few turns franticly (a)pplying my blessed
unicorn horn (which, thankfully, didn't get uncursed). I also could
cast cure sickness at 0% and was near full Pow so that was ok.

Met Eve the invisible Llama. Eve met Stormbringer.

Middle altar was that of Susanowo. Sacrificed the AoY, bated in
radience, wrote my YAAP and went for a drink at the Demigod Bar. :)

